Original GSI routines for the semi-leptonic CC rates (Guo et al. 2020),
from https://git.gsi.de/nucastro_archive/supernovamuonicrates.

  Opacity_SemiLep_2D_GSI.f90   2D integrals (linear Gauss-Legendre in E2 and
                               E3, Ngrids = 50 hardcoded, Tfac = 150)
  Opacity_SemiLep_4D_GSI.f90   4D integrals (Vegas, needs CUBA)

They are kept unchanged and are NOT part of the weaklib library; the unit
tests in Distributions/UnitTests/GeneralEmAb compile them as reference.
Known issues of this copy (fixed in the weaklib modules of ../):
  - Calc_Ampsq clamps |M|^2 >= 0 BEFORE the crossing sign of the inverse
    decay / decay channels is applied (res = -res afterwards), so
    reactions 3 and 4 come out zero (corrections 0-1) or negative (2-3).
  - REAL(4) literals (e.g. 5./7.) in the form-factor block cancel
    catastrophically at large nucleon momentum (correction 3; up to O(1)
    errors for muonic inverse decay / decay).
  - The variance term of the form-factor average (Ic2) is missing.
  - Older constants (Vud = 0.97427, Gf = 1.166e-11): ~6e-4 offset.
  - Results are in km^-1 for reactions 1-3.
